Title: Some Geography!
Author: E. W. Fuller
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-08-09
Notes: A cross-shaped grid, 13 wide and 13 high: a 3-wide arm at top and bottom, a 4-wide arm left and right, AMERICA printed across the middle row as given letters (r7c4-c10). The checkered squares inside the outline are printed as blocks (#). Headline: "SOME GEOGRAPHY! Here's a Perplexing Variety of Cross-Word Puzzle for FUN Readers to Ponder Over." No number is printed on the puzzle; the next week's puzzle calls itself the thirty-second in FUN's series. The text credits it as "a contribution to FUN'S cross-word collection from E. W. Fuller of West Forty-sixth street, New York City." Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_08_09_83.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_08_16_82.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.


